"""Demo data, all fictional, generated by the literature-calibrated simulator (`app.simulator`).

- 12 featured patients (names and stories as before) with region/district/facility, 4 simulated devices each and 60 days
  of readings (HR / SpO2 / skin temperature every 30 min, HRV and breathing rate at night, daily sleep / steps / fluid,
  a few thermometer readings), EMR labs every 2-8 weeks and around bad days, imaging studies with fictional radiology
  reports, crises over 24 months and a daily assessment history.
- A wider registry (`featured=False`, default 1,500 patients across Ghana's 16 regions, weighted by population and
  genotype prevalence) with demographics, hydroxyurea status, crises over 24 months (admission, length of stay,
  facility), the last 14 days of check-ins, the latest lab panel, imaging and a latest assessment each. It feeds the
  policy dashboard. Size: env SEED_REGISTRY_PATIENTS (default 1500 on Postgres, 0 on SQLite so tests stay fast).
- Demo users when DEMO_PASSWORD is set: clinician@, patient@ (linked to Ama Owusu) and policy@sickleguard.local.

Runs only on an empty database (startup, SEED_DEMO=true). Dev reset: `python -m app.seed --reset` wipes the data tables
(keeps users, documents and chunks) and seeds again.
"""
